abstract: >-
  Python program, run from cron or a systemd timer, that checks websites and JSON endpoints and the
  expiry of their TLS certificates, keeps every outage as an incident with its start, end and
  duration in SQLite, and sends grouped email alerts with escalating reminders and a message on
  recovery, through a spare route such as Telegram when the mail cannot be sent. A shell watchdog
  beside it looks every five minutes for the signs of a crypto-miner or a backdoor on the server,
  reporting a busy process only when its load lasts, and mails its findings through the same
  channel.
